  Web-source parity (every branch reproduced — covenant #2 / #5):
    web TONE.live         -> green  dot, no pulse, Activity glyph  -> statusSuccess + waveform.path.ecg
    web TONE.reconnecting -> amber pulse dot,       Wifi  glyph    -> statusWarning + wifi
    web TONE.offline      -> zinc   dot, no pulse,  WifiOff glyph  -> textMuted     + wifi.slash
    web relative(): null->"—"; <5s->"just now"; <60s->"Ns ago"; <60m->"Nm ago"; else "Nh ago"
                    (Math.max(0,…) future-clamp preserved)
    web aria-label "Live status stream: {label}, updated {rel}" -> localized + .updatesFrequently
  States contract: the web leaf is a pure presentational pill fed by its parent
    (useStatusLiveSSE). Its three connection tones ARE its states; the loading/initial
    state = reconnecting + "—" (the web useState seed); empty(no-data) = the "—" stamp;
    stale = the growing relative stamp while the tone stays live (exactly how the web pill
    signals a quiet stream); offline = the offline tone. No fabricated skeleton/error boxes
    (the web source has none — adding them would be drift, covenant #2/#9).

